// A counted `for` in a system runs the `for`s over entities in it so many
// times: once for each layer, with the count in the filter, or in rounds,
// where a reactive `for` reacts to what the round before changed. A
// `loop ... until` runs them until a condition holds.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/for_rounds.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/for_rounds.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      layer 0: 2
// CHECK-NEXT: layer 1: 3
// CHECK-NEXT: layer 2: 1
// The cell that was 1 changed in two rounds, the others in one (being
// new counts as one).
// CHECK-NEXT: 3 3 heard 2
// CHECK-NEXT: 3 3 heard 1
// CHECK-NEXT: 3 3 heard 1
// Raised until none is below 6: three rounds, and one that raises none.
// From 27 to 1 in 111 steps, counted by a `loop` in a fn.
// CHECK-NEXT: 4 rounds, 111 steps
